& [ConstraintLedger] preserves the admissible successor boundary
  + [invariant] is exact source revision exact toolchain and exact build controls are evidence inputs
  + [invariant] is both outputs must be compared by byte length SHA-256 and exact bytes
  + [invariant] is both outputs must preserve the existing effect-free contract field-digest and representative report-verification behavior
  + [prohibition] is no provider request inference call llama.cpp mutation deployment service mutation or report rewrite
  + [prohibition] is no claim that historical h8 was reproducibly produced
  + [boundary_guard] is one Windows host and one toolchain cannot prove cross-host cross-toolchain or production reproducibility
  + [quality_constraint] is any mismatch faults the campaign and withholds a positive receipt

& [SevenFoldExplosion] reaches a phase-locked reversible P0 surface
  + [fold_1_identity] binds Git commit tree archive Cargo.lock toolchain target package profile environment controls and executable identity
  + [fold_2_relationship] requires two separately extracted source roots to originate from the same archived commit and produce one equal output identity
  + [fold_3_condition] admits only a clean archive-built locked offline release campaign with no incremental compilation
  + [fold_4_transformation] permits archive extraction compilation hashing exact comparison and effect-free executable inspection only
  + [fold_5_process] resolve then archive then extract twice then build twice then compare then behavior-check then emit one receipt then clean up
  + [fold_6_evidence] records stable source toolchain control artifact and behavior observations without random temporary paths
  + [fold_7_boundary] stops at local repeatability and preserves deployment cross-machine signature ACL semantic quality and P1 as frontiers
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_reversible_P0

& [BuildCampaignDepthContract] makes the feature actionable
  + [activation_trigger] is an explicit local invocation against a Git revision
  + [actor] is a human or agent with read access to the repository and permission to create temporary files under target
  + [data_subject] is one immutable Git archive two isolated extracted trees two build target directories two executables and one receipt
  + [state_transition] is initialized to source_resolved to source_archived to roots_extracted to builds_completed to artifacts_compared to behavior_verified to receipt_emitted or faulted
  + [service_boundary] is local Git Cargo rustc MSVC linker tar PowerShell and the built field-cycle CLI
  + [policy_gate] is exact revision resolution child-path validation locked offline dependency use and no provider-facing command
  + [proof_gate] is exact byte equality plus equal contract field digest and representative positive control hostile replay verification
  + [lifecycle] is create isolated temporary root use it once emit stable stdout receipt and remove it unless explicit diagnostic retention is requested
  + [failure_mode] is missing tool revision archive extraction compile executable comparison behavior verification or cleanup failure

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] connects every depth component to existing fabric
  + revision and archive identity depend_on the repository Git history and Cargo.lock
  + build controls address FADL_F009 without changing FADL-001 through FADL-013 runtime meanings
  + behavior checks verify the existing contract field and replay interfaces rather than creating a new semantic oracle
  + the receipt supports the P0 proof and operational fault ledger but does not supersede the h8 deployment manifest
  + safe cleanup is constrained by the repository target directory and OperationalFaults discipline

& [Delineation] separates three identities that must not collapse
  + [content_identity] is the SHA-256 and bytes of one executable
  + [local_reproduction_identity] is equality of two clean outputs under the recorded local campaign
  + [deployment_identity] is an independently copied and reverified executable under a deployment trust boundary
  - never: infer deployment identity from local reproduction identity
  - never: infer general reproducibility from one host and toolchain

& [DualHemisphereReview] preserves holistic utility and exact proof
  + the receptive reading is a one-command answer to whether the current source can repeat locally under explicit controls
  + the analytic reading requires exact source isolation controls bytes behaviors failure states and claim boundaries
  + integration keeps the command convenient while making every positive statement falsifiable

& [PruningTrace] records rejected growth
  + remote-host comparison is pruned to a future cross-machine campaign
  + production signing ACL repair and artifact deployment are pruned to trust-root work
  + provider calls and semantic-quality measurement are pruned because they are unnecessary effects
  + generalized Cargo workspace reproducibility is pruned because this slice targets cantor_field_cycle only
  + historical h8 reproduction is rejected because its original build environment was not preserved as this profile

& [GrowthSeedSet] preserves honest successors
  + compare this profile across two independently provisioned Windows hosts
  + bind a production signing identity and protected deployment root
  + decide whether a new reproducibly built artifact should supersede h8 under separate deployment authority

& [Falsification] is immediate and inspectable
  + different executable bytes fail
  + different contract output or field digest fails
  + failure of either executable to verify any selected retained report fails
  + source or tool identity that cannot be recorded fails
  + inability to constrain cleanup to the campaign root fails closed
